bot%2F79267492faab096d04cdd25ce7014cec%2Fraw%2Fmacos-15-arm64.json) | arm64 | `macos-15`, or `macos-15-xlarge` | [macOS-15-arm64] |\\n42:### Label scheme\\n44:- In general the `-latest` label is used for the latest OS image version that is GA.\\n45:- Before moving the `-latest` label to a new OS version we will announce the change and give sufficient lead time for users to update their workflows.\\n46:- The `-xlarge` and `-large` suffixes are unique to macOS images and are only available for GitHub Actions. Learn more about [GitHub Actions larger runners](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/runners/larger-runners#available-macos-larger-runners-and-labels).\\n61:[macOS-15]: https://github.com/actions/runner-images/blob/main/images/macos/macos-15-Readme.md\\n62:[macOS-15-arm64]: https://github.com/actions/runner-images/blob/main/images/macos/macos-15-arm64-Readme.md\\n63:[macOS-26]: https://github.com/actions/runner-images/blob/main/images/macos/macos-26-Readme.md\\n64:[macOS-26-arm64]: https://github.com/actions/runner-images/blob/main/images/macos/macos-26-arm64-Readme.md\\n70:See notable upcoming changes by viewing issues with the [Announcement](https://github.com/actions/runner-images/labels/Announcement) label.\\n95:GitHub Actions and Azure DevOps use the `-latest` YAML label (ex: `ubuntu-latest`, `windows-latest`, and `macos-latest`). These labels point towards the newest stable OS version available.\\n97:The `-latest` migration process is gradual and happens over 1-2 months in order to allow customers to adapt their workflows to the newest OS version. During this process, any workflow using the `-latest` label, may see changes in the OS version in their workflows or pipelines. To avoid unwanted migration, users can specify a specific OS version in the yaml file (ex: macos-14, windows-2022, ubuntu-22.04).\\n107:   - You can also track upcoming changes using the [awaiting-deployment](https://github.com/actions/runner-images/labels/awaiting-deployment) label.\\n120:- We support (at maximum) 2 GA images and 1 beta image at a time. We begin the deprecation process of the oldest image label once the newest OS image label has been released to GA.\\n155:- Images begin the deprecation process of the oldest image label once a new GA OS version has been released.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3308,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 827,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
