all captured **without\\n431:independently snapshotted from the selected base and present worktree. It is\\n436:snapshot, so the recorded base is also the stable input to later re-parenting\\n440:Story-scoped and the snapshotter has no durable per-task path ownership model.\\n461:`conflicted` — keep refusing whatever their delta is, because the next snapshot\\n548:reviewer-archetype run bound to this element and this revision; an untracked\\n933:that its omitted lane paths are untracked and ignored. An extra local commit,\\n938:reviewed source snapshot is preserved; the temporary integration index carries\\n1416:provenance, then explicitly spawn with the same class transport, fresh snapshot\\n1483:`claude-haiku-4-5` (10); its dated snapshot shares rank 10.\\n1487:immutable rollout snapshot, not this mutable rank ladder. Legacy IDs remain\\n1490:`claude-fable-5-1` was registered after that rollout snapshot was captured, so\\n1504:changing either the v2 snapshot or any v3 set. Use target-only `project_config`\\n1842:history. Use `status` for a diagnostic snapshot, `events` for replay, `watch`\\n1893:already contains an exact caller snapshot.\\n1977:Producer provider exit is not handoff success. A `role_handoff` run must reach its immutable role end status and add or update a task-scoped outcome artifact relative to its launch snapshot. Zero exit while the board remains in `analysis`/`development`, or at the handoff status without evidence, queues autonomous same-revision recovery.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 2402,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 601,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
